glibc headers (linux-x64 kit only)
  Upstream: the build host's libc6-dev package (Debian/Ubuntu)
  License:  as stated in that package's own copyright file
  Location: <payload>/kit/sysroot/usr/include/, license text at
            <payload>/kit/licenses/libc6-dev-copyright.txt
  Note:     headers only, not linked into any mcppls binary.

Linux kernel headers (linux-x64 kit only)
  Upstream: the build host's linux-libc-dev package (Debian/Ubuntu)
  License:  as stated in that package's own copyright file
  Location: <payload>/kit/sysroot/usr/include/, license text at
            <payload>/kit/licenses/linux-libc-dev-copyright.txt
  Note:     headers only, not linked into any mcppls binary. A handful of files whose names
            differ only in case (e.g. xt_mark.h / xt_MARK.h) are kept under their all-lowercase
            name only; packaging/kits/README.md and mcppls.pack.kit record what was dropped.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The macOS kit (darwin-arm64) carries no bundled C library headers: Apple's SDK license does not
allow redistributing them, so that kit requires the macOS SDK already installed on the machine
(Xcode or the Command Line Tools) and uses it in place.
